    "created_at": "2020-09-11T00:30:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-11T00:30:32Z",
    "body": "I don't have a strong opinion. Putting it in `.connect()` makes it impossible to change later in the lifetime of the connection, which is probably easier implementation-wise, and I don't immediately see any use cases that couldn't handle that.",
